  "worked_solution": "If $Z\u223cN(0,1),$ then by the definition of the cumulative distribution function $\u03a6(z),$ \n\n$$\nP(Z\\le z)=\u03a6(z).\n$$\n\nAlso, since $Z$ is continuous, \n\n$$\nP(Z<-0.35)=P(Z\\le -0.35)=\u03a6(-0.35).\n$$\n\nThe required probability is represented by the area shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069404/assets/ab5be5e655c8daad36f35bee1abf3c82e3766b734da928be3dd060db551fbbb9.png)\n\nNow, we determine the value of $\u03a6(-0.35)$ from the table:\n\n- We first select the row that corresponds to $-0.3$ and the column that corresponds to $0.05.$\n\n- Then, we take the value that lies at the intersection:\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.05\\,$ | $\\,0.06\\,$ | $\\,0.07\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,-0.4\\,$ | $\\,0.3264\\,$ | $\\,0.3228\\,$ | $\\,0.3192\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.3\\,$ | $\\,0.3632\\,$ | $\\,0.3594\\,$ | $\\,0.3557\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.2\\,$ | $\\,0.4013\\,$ | $\\,0.3974\\,$ | $\\,0.3936\\,$ |\n\nTherefore, according to the table, we have\n\n$$\nP(Z\\le -0.35)=\u03a6(-0.35)=0.3632.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
